delay, but a seller who misses an agreed dispatch date or repeatedly fails to answer a required specification question deserves review. Check the order message history before contacting support, then provide the order number, current status, promised date, and the exact decision you need. This turns “Why is it slow?” into a request the team can investigate."
      ],
      [
        "Answer seller questions in one complete message",
        "Agent-assisted buying places a communication layer between buyer and seller. Each back-and-forth can add delay, so answer every open point in one message. Repeat the order number, exact variation, acceptable price limit when relevant, and the action you authorize.\n\nA useful reply might say: “Order X: buy size M in black only. Gray is not acceptable. Approve the stated domestic shipping; cancel if black is unavailable.” This is better than several separate messages that leave the agent to assemble your decision.\n\nSet limits before the seller changes the deal. Decide whether you accept a price adjustment, delayed dispatch, alternative color, revised domestic freight, or partial stock. For multi-quantity purchases, ask whether the full quantity is available.\n\nKeep communication factual. Screenshots, listing text, and exact option names resolve problems better than accusations. The seller controls stock and transaction approval, while clear evidence gives Sugargoo a stronger basis for acting on your behalf."
      ],
      [
        "Audit warehouse arrival against the original brief",
        "Sugargoo’s current official materials say the seller sends the product to its warehouse, where inspection is performed and five free product photos are provided before international shipping. Compare those images with the brief saved before purchase.\n\nCheck identity first: product type, color, size label, quantity, and visible accessories. Then check condition: obvious damage, stains, deformation, major construction defects, or packaging problems. If a measurement or close-up is needed, request it precisely. “Photo of the size tag and a tape measurement from shoulder seam to hem” is actionable; “more QC” is not.\n\nQC photos do not prove authenticity, long-term durability, fit, or every internal function. Use them for visible questions and decide promptly while a domestic remedy may still be possible. Keep any disputed item out of parcel submission. Consolidating it can turn a solvable warehouse issue into an expensive international 